CANONICAL reference digest for the frozen preregistration, superseding the value recorded in
PREREG_P2_v2.sha256 and in the document's own section 12.

Procedure (as shipped in PREREG_P2_v2.md section 12):
    LF-normalised UTF-8 bytes, with the `sha256:` line substituted by the 64-hex placeholder
    f25b842a1fed9c52d92a04018af35fc1f79bc30f562adb3711ec3a5f165a9ffe

Why this file exists: the previously recorded digest b3f5fb3c... is not reproducible from the
frozen text under any normalisation, and corresponds to no committed state of the document. It
was computed on an uncommitted intermediate draft and not recomputed after subsequent edits.
The document CONTENT is unchanged and provably so -- the working file is byte-identical to
freeze commit 7980d489 and git reports it unmodified.

Note: PREREG_P2_v2.md section 12's PROSE specifies a different placeholder (`<pending>`), under
which the digest is 1c97fb1bdd1e5b9c76c60e4d6df756fddd37b5fa0a834d81909807b8dde44eb6. That
convention is the one under which PREREG_P2.md (v1) reproduces its recorded digest
8ac3895709be0721656cef0c705cf843302245ab6d841373ee1676032db203e9 exactly. The value at the top
of this file follows section 12's CODE, so that a reader running the shipped snippet gets it.

Neither PREREG_P2_v2.md nor PREREG_P2_v2.sha256 was altered. Full provenance is in STATUS.md
under "PREREG DIGEST DISCREPANCY: RESOLVED", dated 2026-09-07.
